https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8AHCfZTRGiI  (Capo 0) (MC0)

TIP:  It’s a little tricky to get the strumming down.  The verse is mostly single downstrums, with a down-up-down-up on the cord that ends each line/phrase.  The verse ends with a basic down-up-down strum pattern and continue through the chorus.  Hard to describe but you should hear it readily.  I find the verse easier to fingerpick than strum.  Try pinching pairs of strings, or “stabbing” the middle strings, while moving through the chords.  Should be able to get something that sounds decent.

TIP:  The verse starts with a two-count of (CaddG) followed by (C).  Since (CaddG) is just a regular (C) with your pinky added to the 1st string/3rd fret all you do is start with (CaddG) and then lift off the pinky and you’re at (C).  Suggest single downstrums for these first three chords.  Or if you prefer, just ignore the (CaddG) and play (C).

TIP:  John ends the song with a single strum of |G| but sings the final word on an <a> note.  I’ve added an additional strum of |Am| on “way.”
    

